      "rule": "R19",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The acceptance rule says an unknown clock or counter ends a plain INSERT, but a literal INSERT can continue without a clock and with unknown counters when it reads neither. Fix: State that the run ends at these checks when `statementClock` returns `none` or `Counters.firstUnknown` finds an unknown counter among `resolved.counterReads`."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261123T141553Z-13640dbc#2",
      "line": 228,
      "path": "plans/20261123-statement-rule-pilot.task.md",
      "rule": "R19",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The task says `runStatement` returns a run that is not ready for a missing target, but that branch sets `ready := true` and returns an `.unmodeled` effect. Fix: State that the missing target ends the step through `Output.ofStep`, and reserve readiness failures for the three checks on a present target."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261123T141553Z-13640dbc#3",
      "line": 270,
      "path": "plans/20261123-statement-rule-pilot.task.md",
      "rule": "R19",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The blanket prohibition on adding imports conflicts with the requirement for two new Lean fixtures that use the pilot laws and must import modules exposing them. Fix: Limit the prohibition to new external dependencies and imports outside the permitted package boundaries."
    }
